**How to implement.** Experiments are named by the kit's template and stored as `<name>.experiment-json` (001 §A kit layout `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL.experiment-json`; 001 §J the template names setups and experiments; the S9.1 brief; the S6 mapper's request: `renumberedFor`'s rule carries over to names; the S8.4 mapper's request: the slot bar's `RecordExperiment` names its experiment by the template). This is one step because the record gains a field every consumer builds. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: (a) `Experiment` gains `name : ExperimentName` after `id`, and `ExperimentId.fileStem` (step 146) is deleted: the stem is the name's (step 286). (b) `ExperimentTarget = { setup : SetupReference; name : ExperimentName }`, one experiment to append: its setup revision and its name. `commit (target : ExperimentTarget) (c : ExperimentCollection)` names an appended experiment `target.name` over `target.setup`; an edited experiment takes `target.setup` and keeps its name, so an experiment is never renamed by an edit. `commitOverSetups (targets : ExperimentTarget list)` folds it over the targets in order, as step 275's fold over references. (c) `static member renamedFor (taken : ExperimentName list) (incoming : Experiment list) : Experiment list` on `Experiment`, beside step 203's `renumberedFor`: in order, an incoming experiment keeps its name when no name of `taken` and no name given to an earlier incoming experiment has its `fileStem` ignoring case; otherwise it takes `name.nextFreeAmong` of those; only `name` changes. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/NamingTemplates.fs`, after step 286's member: `type NamingTemplate with member this.experimentTargets (setups : Setup list) (items : Item list) (taken : ExperimentName list) (firstId : ExperimentId) : ExperimentTarget list`: for each setup in order, the target of its `reference` named by `experimentNameAmong setup.slots items None (taken followed by the names given so far) id.defaultName`, `id` starting at `firstId` and advancing by `next` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentId`), so the unnamed fallback is the id the experiment receives. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 148, 224, 261): `writeExperiment` writes `ExperimentKitFile` under `experiment.name.fileStem`; `deleteExperiment (name : ExperimentName)` deletes `name.fileStem`; `readExperiments` refuses, as `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file, a file whose experiment's `name.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case (it compared `id.fileStem`); and `copyExperimentsFrom`, after `renumberedFor`, applies `renamedFor` over the names of `this.proxy.readExperiments ()`, an id the source lacks still being `MissingKitFileErr` of the `ExperimentKitFile` name of its `defaultName`'s stem, so its texts are unchanged. `schema/experiment.schema.json` requires `name`, a string holding a non-white-space character, after `id`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: the private function that records the experiments a commit appended (step 278) is unchanged; the three callers name what they append through `model.kit.kitFile.namingTemplate.experimentTargets` (step 267) over the setups they commit over, `model.kitItems`, the names of `model.experimentCollection.experiments` and the collection's `nextId`: `ExpCommit` appending over the recorded setup (an edit passes the target of that setup and keeps the name), `RecordExperiment` over the active setup and `GenerateSetupGrid` over the generated setups, each then calling `commit` / `commitOverSetups` with the targets. `ExpRemove` deletes the removed experiment's file through `deleteExperiment` of its name. `RecordExperiment`'s status names the experiment, `Recorded <name.value> over <reference.describe>.`, which for a table the template cannot name is today's `Recorded E2 over 'Bench' revision 1.`. (5) Every fixture that builds an `Experiment` sets `name = <its id>.defaultName`, so every file it writes keeps its `E<n>` name and every fact its assertions (the files of step 288's list). Tests. `KitContentFileJsonTests`: `an experiment is stored under its id` is renamed `an experiment is stored under its name`: `ExperimentKitFile.fileNameOf (ExperimentName "CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL").fileStem` is `FileName "CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL.experiment-json"` and `(ExperimentId 3).defaultName.fileStem` is `FileStem "E3"`; its schema fact also refuses an experiment without `name` and one whose `name` is `"  "`. `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`: `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another id, refuses the read, naming the file` is renamed `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the read, naming the file`, its second file holding E1 under the stem `E6` (another name). `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `copied experiments keep their names unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free suffix`: with `taken` [`CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`], incoming experiments named `cpl-(qz#45)-cpl` and `E3` answer `cpl-(qz#45)-cpl (2)` and `E3`, in that order; with `taken` empty they are unchanged; every field but `name` is unchanged; its commit facts pass targets named by `defaultName`, their assertions kept. `NamingTemplateTests` gains `the experiments of new setups are named by the template over each setup's slots, each free among the kit's and the earlier ones`: `lab`'s targets over the setups `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL` and `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL` (made from step 271's slots) with `taken` [`CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL`] and `firstId` E4 are `CPL-(QZ#45)-CPL (2)` and `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL`, each over its setup's reference, and over a setup the template cannot name the first is `E4`. `ExperimentCopyTests` (steps 224, 227, 261) gains `a copied experiment whose name the target holds takes the next free name`: copying [E1] into a target holding an experiment named `E1` (another id) writes the copy as `E1 (2).experiment-json` and the report names it so. `SetupModelTests`: `a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name` (step 272) also finds `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.experiment-json`, E1 being named so; `GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each` (step 276) finds `LP1-(QZ#0)-LPd.experiment-json` and `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.experiment-json` in place of `E1` and `E2`; and `a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing` finds the second run's experiments as `LP1-(QZ#0)-LPd (2)` and `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd (2)`. Every other fact, the UI facts that find `E<n>.experiment-json` included, passes as written, because their tables hold no item the template needs.

**Acceptance.** After experiments are named, `Experiment.name` MUST be the file stem every experiment is written, read, deleted and copied under, a new experiment MUST be named by the kit's template over its setup (made free) or `E<n>`, and a copied experiment whose name the target holds MUST take the next free name; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `copied experiments keep their names unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free suffix`, `the experiments of new setups are named by the template over each setup's slots, each free among the kit's and the earlier ones` and `a copied experiment whose name the target holds takes the next free name`, the count rising by 3, the renamed `an experiment is stored under its name` and `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the read, naming the file` and the changed `a commit on a table the kit's template names records it under that name`, `GenerateSetupGrid records a setup per ticked combination, named by the kit's template, and an experiment of the draft over each` and `a grid over setups the kit holds writes no setup again, and a grid it cannot make writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
